    "text": "```python\nimport csv\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n\ndef load_rows(path):\n    \"\"\"Load CSV rows from the given file path.\"\"\"\n    rows = []\n    with open(path, newline=\"\") as f:\n        reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n        for row in reader:\n            rows.append(row)\n    return rows\n\n\ndef sum_by_region(rows):\n    \"\"\"Sum amounts by region from the given rows.\"\"\"\n    total = defaultdict(float)\n    for row in rows:\n        region = row[\"region\"].strip().title()\n        amount = float(row[\"amount\"])\n        total[region] += amount\n    return dict(total)\n\n\ndef top_regions(rows, n=3):\n    \"\"\"Return the top n regions by total amount.\"\"\"\n    total = sum_by_region(rows)\n    ranked = sorted(total.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1], reverse=True)\n    return ranked[:n]\n\n\ndef monthly_totals(rows):\n    \"\"\"Compute monthly totals from the given rows.\"\"\"\n    total = defaultdict(float)\n    for row in rows:\n        month = row[\"date\"][:7]\n        total[month] += float(row[\"amount\"])\n    return dict(sorted(total.items()))\n\n\ndef report(path):\n    \"\"\"Generate and print a sales report from the given file path.\"\"\"\n    rows = load_rows(path)\n    total = top_regions(rows)\n    for region, amount in total:\n        print(f\"{region:<12} {amount:>10.2f}\")\n    for month, amount in monthly_totals(rows).items():\n        print(f\"{month}  {amount:>10.2f}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    report(\"sales.csv\")\n```",
